Also, if you would like to send us a letter about your relationship to the show, how it's affected you and what it's meant to you over the years, or if you want to drop us a voice note that maybe we could read at the or play at the beginning of the show, go to our square space created website energy how we made your mother dot com h w w m y m h dot m y m dot com go to contact and it should be pretty clear from there because square space makes everything pretty clear and Alec did a great job with that here is today's letter hi Josh I wanted to say thank you.
另外，如果你想给我们写信，谈谈你与这部剧的缘分、它如何影响了你以及这些年来它对你的意义，或者如果你想给我们留下一条语音留言，也许我们可以在节目开始时朗读或播放，请访问我们用Squarespace创建的网站 energy how we made your mother dot com h w w m y m h dot m y m dot com，点击联系我们，从那里看应该非常清楚，因为Squarespace把一切都弄得很清楚，亚历克在这方面做得很好，这是今天的信：嗨，乔希，我想说谢谢你。

00:46:34.086 --> 00:46:40.942
I watched liberal arts in 2015, that's a movie I wrote and directed, and recommended it to my friends.
我在2015年观看了《裂缝》（Liberal Arts），那是我编剧并导演的一部电影，并把它推荐给了我的朋友们。

00:46:40.942 --> 00:46:47.261
When they saw the movie, they went, that's Ted Mosby Shantanu, and I had no idea who that was.
当他们看到这部电影时，他们说，那是泰德·莫斯比·尚塔努，而我当时根本不知道那是谁。

00:46:47.261 --> 00:46:55.328
After about a year of wondering whether I should even start watching movies or TV shows, I was completely new to cinema.
在大约一年的时间里，我一直在纠结自己是否应该开始看电影或电视剧，我对电影界完全是个新人。

00:46:55.328 --> 00:46:57.009
I thought, you know what?
我想，你知道吗？

00:46:57.009 --> 00:46:59.630
Let's give how I met your mother a try.
让我们试着看一看《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:46:59.630 --> 00:47:00.706
All caps hooked.
全部大写，入坑了。

00:47:00.706 --> 00:47:02.050
It was unbelievable.
这太不可思议了。

00:47:02.050 --> 00:47:07.159
I'd never seen someone disguise such as serious drama as a comedy like that.
我从未见过有人能把如此严肃的戏剧伪装成这样一部喜剧。

00:47:07.159 --> 00:47:13.814
After the show ended, I watched the cast interviews, the bloopers, basically anything I could find.
剧集结束后，我观看了演员采访、花絮，基本上是所有能找到的东西。

00:47:13.814 --> 00:47:18.990
That's when I started hearing your thoughts on fame, happiness, and humanity.
也就是在那时，我开始听到你对名誉、幸福和人性的看法。

00:47:18.990 --> 00:47:22.150
Apart from my dad, I have two male role models.
除了我爸爸，我有两个男性榜样。

00:47:22.150 --> 00:47:25.914
One is you, and the other is Maddie Healy from the 1975.
一个是您，另一个是来自1975乐队（The 1975）的马蒂·希利（Maddie Healy）。

00:47:25.914 --> 00:47:29.880
Thank you for showing me that my thoughts are not who I am.
感谢您让我明白，我的想法并不代表真正的我。

00:47:29.880 --> 00:47:31.090
My actions aren't.
我的行动也不代表。

00:47:31.090 --> 00:47:36.468
I had to limit my social media usage to two days a month to really live by that.
为了真正践行这一点，我不得不将社交媒体的使用限制为一个月两天。

00:47:36.468 --> 00:47:46.888
Watching the world split itself into left versus right, I've realized it's better for me to just shut up, do my job, and take care of the people around me.
看着世界分裂为左派和右派，我意识到对我来说最好的做法就是闭嘴，做好我的工作，照顾好我身边的人。

00:47:46.888 --> 00:47:51.324
I want my music, the art I'm building to not be about that divide.
我希望我的音乐，我正在创作的艺术，不要与那种分裂有关。

00:47:51.324 --> 00:47:53.274
I want it to be for everyone.
我希望它是为所有人而作的。

00:47:53.274 --> 00:47:59.257
I now spend a lot of effort trying to understand someone's intent before I say something.
我现在花了很多精力在开口说话之前去理解别人的意图。

00:47:59.257 --> 00:48:02.349
It's tough to do in my head, but I'll be okay.
在脑子里做这件事很难，但我会没事的。

00:48:02.349 --> 00:48:02.849
I know.
我知道。

00:48:02.820 --> 00:48:05.539
Happy, thank you more, please, Shuntan.
祝我快乐，请多指教，尚塔努。

00:48:05.539 --> 00:48:06.980
Thanks for that.
谢谢你的来信。

00:48:06.980 --> 00:48:07.980
That's lovely.
真可爱。

00:48:07.980 --> 00:48:08.980
That's wonderful.
太棒了。

00:48:08.980 --> 00:48:15.460
You know, I really love this observation, a serious drama disguised as a comedy.
你知道，我真的很喜欢这个观察，一部伪装成喜剧的严肃戏剧。

00:48:15.460 --> 00:48:16.460
That's the show.
节目就是这样。

00:48:16.460 --> 00:48:18.980
I thought that was a really wonderful observation.
我觉得那是一个非常精彩的观察。

00:48:18.980 --> 00:48:19.980
Yeah.
是的。

00:48:19.980 --> 00:48:20.980
Me too.
我也是。

00:48:20.980 --> 00:48:21.980
I love that way of framing it.
我很喜欢这种表述方式。

00:48:21.980 --> 00:48:22.980
That's how we think of it.
我们就是这么想的。

00:48:22.980 --> 00:48:31.219
And that's the Trojan horse we were sneaking on to CBS in 2005 among a lot of other sitcoms or sitcoms.
这也是我们在2005年与其他许多情景喜剧一起潜入CBS的木马计。

00:48:31.219 --> 00:48:32.219
I would say.
我得这么说。

00:48:32.219 --> 00:48:33.219
I don't even mean that as an insult.
我甚至不是在讽刺。

00:48:33.219 --> 00:48:38.219
different tones, and we were kind of, we were our own little thing, and that's what we were, so thanks for seeing it.
不同的基调，我们有点像我们自己的小天地，我们就是那样的，所以谢谢你能看出来。

00:48:38.219 --> 00:48:40.610
Yeah, thanks so much.
是的，非常感谢。

00:48:40.610 --> 00:48:49.300
I am guilty, please equip me, all sins are forgiven, in New York City.
我有罪，请惩罚我吧，在纽约市，所有的罪孽都被原谅了。

